__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.zip
*.7z
*.dll
*.addon64
*.addon32
*.exe
*.log
*.log.*
*.png.bak
_dlss5_proton_backup/
_dlss5_proton_state.json
_dlss5_proton_dlls.json
.cache/
discord/
notes/
memory/
*.bak-*

# The AppImage build. packaging/ is the recipe and is committed; build/ is the
# downloaded interpreter, the wheels and the AppDir, and the artefact is 134 MB.
# packaging/pins.lock is NOT ignored - it is what makes a build reproducible.
build/
*.AppImage
*.AppImage.zsync

# The test fixtures are named after exactly what the rules above keep out: the
# old tool's real state file, and real logs. These are neither - they are small,
# invented, and the suite cannot run without them. A clean clone got one of the
# five, which nobody noticed until CI became the first thing ever to run the
# tests somewhere other than a machine that already had them.
!tests/fixtures/_dlss5_proton_state.json
!tests/fixtures/logs/*.log
